      "writtenOn": "2018-02-16T11:18:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually, Aaron\u0027s comment now looks totally different from what I thought...   If we separate BOARD_VERSION into two 1-byte fields, we lose advantage of handling version as an integer. I\u0027m guessing most callers just do numeric comparison with BOARD_VERSION as a whole. If it\u0027s separated, it takes two host command calls.\n\nRegarding tag v.s. field length: We shouldn\u0027t (or don\u0027t need to) bind semantics to the field length. Tags hold the semantics. As long as the tag is the same, the field lengths shouldn\u0027t matter. Of course 1-byte field can\u0027t describe a tuple field (e.g. minor:major version). So, it\u0027s necessary to bump up the field length but the other way should be permitted (a long field describes a short value).",
      "parentUuid": "3c1a2b84_cdea9381",
